      "schema": "schema/countries.schema.json",
      "title": "Local service numbers & country info",
      "kind": "static",
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "European Commission — 112, the single EU emergency number (police/fire/medical)",
          "url": "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/112"
        },
        {
          "name": "UK FCDO foreign travel advice (per-country 'getting help')",
          "url": "https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"
        },
        {
          "name": "US State Dept — country information & emergency contacts",
          "url": "https://travel.state.gov/en/international-travel.html"
        },
        {
          "name": "National emergency authorities (per-entry 'source' field cites the specific government reference)",
          "url": null
        }
      ],
      "lastUpdated": "2026-09-06",
      "lastChecked": "2026-09-06",
      "staleAfterDays": 90,
      "sha256": "ce11f340ccd17a6dca34e8be95fc835d0a93a9884aa29a38d960bbe69d59490e",
      "needsVerification": true,
      "note": "Government references are recorded per entry and shown in-app. All 50 entries had an automated source comparison on 2026-07-12; no independent verification is claimed. On 2026-09-06, automated comparison added national EU access codes with routing/regional captions, South Africa mobile-only 112, and reconciled Indonesia to national authorities (110/119/113; no nationwide 112 claim). The content-update date also covers metadata edits; it does not mean every service number was rechecked that day. See docs/data/REVIEW-2026-09-06.md for evidence and scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "embassies",
      "file": "embassies.json",
      "schema": "schema/embassies.schema.json",
      "title": "Embassy addresses & phone numbers",
      "kind": "static",
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "US embassies directory",
          "url": "https://www.usembassy.gov"
        },
        {
          "name": "UK embassies directory (gov.uk)",
          "url": "https://www.gov.uk/world/embassies"
        },
        {
          "name": "Canadian embassies directory",
          "url": "https://travel.gc.ca/assistance/embassies-consulates"
        },
        {
          "name": "Australian embassies (DFAT)",
          "url": "https://www.dfat.gov.au/about-us/our-locations/missions/our-embassies-and-consulates-overseas",
          "verifyUrl": false
        },
        {
          "name": "New Zealand embassies (MFAT)",
          "url": "https://www.mfat.govt.nz/en/countries-and-regions/"
        },
        {
          "name": "Ireland embassies (DFA)",
          "url": "https://www.dfa.ie/embassies/"
        }
      ],
      "lastUpdated": "2026-09-06",
      "lastChecked": "2026-09-06",
      "staleAfterDays": 180,
      "sha256": "39ae8c98e04fe26231da9107650a240d24399b4478e6542dc0c2d945901ef7df",
      "needsVerification": true,
      "note": "Live-first (#56): the authoritative source for every nationality×destination pair is the government embassy directory (link) + a live Apple Maps lookup, shown in-app for all pairs. A small set of records (US/GB/CA/AU in FR/JP/MX/TH) is bundled for offline reference and is always cross-linked to the official directory to verify. No embassy detail is fabricated. On 2026-09-06, US/MX address, main telephone and U.S. citizen-service hours were updated from the current embassy page and State Dept following the 2025 relocation. The obsolete map coordinate was removed; this record uses runtime geocoding of the current address. See docs/data/REVIEW-2026-09-06.md for evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "phrases",
      "file": "phrases.json",
      "schema": "schema/phrases.schema.json",
      "title": "Translation phrases",
      "kind": "static",
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "JourneyMate editorial — AI-drafted translations; not independently verified",
          "url": null
        }
      ],
      "lastUpdated": "2026-09-06",
      "lastChecked": "2026-09-06",
      "staleAfterDays": 365,
      "sha256": "f49266b2283e8089ba159a0874d44b545047576e74b87ab6609eec1c72040a8b",
      "needsVerification": true,
      "note": "Covers all 50 destination languages (#64) via same-language fallback (es-ES→es-MX, etc.). AI-drafted phrases with romanization for non-Latin scripts; not independently verified. Speaker-gender revision 2026-09-06 (#85): pl-PL, cs-CZ and hr-HR use masculine/feminine past-tense alternatives for accident/passport phrases, preserving first-person meaning without defaulting to a male speaker. he-IL uses required-service constructions without assigning gender to the speaker, with updated romanization; its accident/passport past forms were already speaker-neutral. Dual forms are displayed with a slash; speech output may pronounce both alternatives. See docs/data/REVIEW-2026-09-06.md for phrase notes."
    },
    {
      "id": "alerts",
      "file": null,
      "title": "Travel & weather alerts",
      "kind": "runtime",
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "Apple Weather (WeatherKit) — severe weather alerts",
